  "raw_text": "No. A 10% sales decline alone doesn’t prove the marketing campaign failed.\n\nYou’d need to compare sales against a credible baseline—such as a control group, prior-year seasonality, or a forecast without the campaign—and consider factors like pricing, inventory, competitors, economic conditions, and campaign timing. Also assess campaign-specific metrics such as reach, conversions, customer acquisition cost, and incremental revenue.\n\nIt’s possible sales would have fallen more without the campaign. The right question is whether the campaign produced **incremental sales or profit relative to what would otherwise have happened**.",
